<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yeshaq (Bahr Negash)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1578</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yeshaq was Bahr Negash, governor of the northern province of Medri Bahri in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, in the mid-sixteenth century. He supported Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/galawdewos">Gelawdewos</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> but later rebelled and allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> of the Habesh Eyalet against the Ethiopian emperors. He was killed in 1578 in battle against the forces of Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarsa-dengel">Sarsa Dengel</a>.</p></div>
